Step-by-Step Guide: Download & Run the Project
Prerequisites — Install These First
1. Install Git
•	Download from: https://git-scm.com/download/win
•	Run the installer with default settings
•	Verify: open Command Prompt and type git --version
2. Install Node.js
•	Download from: https://nodejs.org (choose the LTS version)
•	Run the installer with default settings
•	Verify: node --version and npm --version
3. Install MySQL
•	Download MySQL Community Server from: https://dev.mysql.com/downloads/mysql/
•	During setup, set a root password (remember it!)
•	Also install MySQL Workbench (optional, but helpful for viewing data)

Step 1 — Clone the Repository
Open Command Prompt and run:
git clone https://github.com/vyshnavimunja/Secure_Student_Portal.git
cd Secure_Student_Portal

Step 2 — Install Dependencies
cd securesp/backend
npm install

Step 3 — Create the .env File
Inside the securesp/backend/ folder, create a file named .env (no extension) with this content:
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_mysql_password_here
DB_NAME=securesp_db
DB_PORT=3306

JWT_SECRET=any_long_random_string_here
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=another_long_random_string_here
PORT=3000
Replace your_mysql_password_here with the password you set during MySQL installation.

Step 4 — Create the MySQL Database
Open MySQL Workbench or MySQL Command Line and run:
CREATE DATABASE securesp_db;
The app will automatically create all tables when it first starts.

Step 5 — (Optional) Seed Sample Data
npm run seed
This loads sample users and courses into the database so you have data to work with right away.

Step 6 — Start the Server
npm start
You should see:
  Initialising database…
  Database ready.

  Secure Student Portal
  URL:  http://localhost:3000
  Env:  development
  
  Run seed: npm run seed

Step 7 — Open the App
Open your browser and go to:
http://localhost:3000
The backend serves both the API and all frontend pages from a single server. There is no separate frontend step.

Quick Troubleshooting

Problem	Fix
npm: command not found	Node.js not installed — redo Step 2
Cannot connect to database	MySQL not running, or wrong password in .env
Port 3000 already in use	Change PORT=3001 in .env
npm install errors	Delete node_modules folder and run npm install again

That's it! The backend runs at http://localhost:3000 and the frontend is opened directly as an HTML file in your browser.

